sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch10-18> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Minimal Boolean formulas (in disjunctive normal form or in Nand operations) for the outcome of rule 30 grow rapidly with the number of steps, unlike those for simple rules such as 90 and 254, indicating that no simple formula describes rule 30 evolution and that, in most cases, cellular automaton patterns have no simple mathematical formula.";
    dc:type "computational-observation";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "No simple formula describes many steps of rule 30 evolution";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 10, “Processes of Perception and Analysis”; section “Human Thinking” (from p. 620), p. 620. Scope: formula representations of cellular automaton evolution, especially rule 30"
}
